Author: LENA-integration-agent <lena-integration-agent@users.noreply.local>
Date:   Mon Oct 19 09:13:01 2026 +0000

    test(refunds): pin payment_mismatch — a foreign payment is refused and writes nothing
    
    The per-sale refund lock (d90b7c9) covers every refund of a sale only because
    createRefund refuses a payment that does not belong to the named sale
    (payment_mismatch). Nothing tested that check: deleting it left every test green.
    
    G (real PG, same file, skipped without NILE_TEST_PG_ADMIN_URL): two sales of
    the same item, one card, one cash in an open shift. Naming each sale with the
    other's payment — sequentially and concurrently — is refused with
    payment_mismatch, and tenant-wide refund rows, refund stock movements, item
    stock and the shift's cash movements are unchanged; each sale can still refund
    its unit through its own payment afterwards.
    
    Mutation check: with the payment_mismatch line removed, G fails ("promise
    resolved instead of rejecting"); A-F still pass. Test-only, no logic change.

diff --git a/engines/transactions/test/refund-concurrency.pg.test.ts b/engines/transactions/test/refund-concurrency.pg.test.ts
index 8958d86..661be2e 100644
--- a/engines/transactions/test/refund-concurrency.pg.test.ts
